1
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:07,080
[Fragments of Truth]

2
00:01:07,080 --> 00:01:08,600
[Episode 18]

3
00:01:09,920 --> 00:01:10,950
[Six years ago]

4
00:01:11,870 --> 00:01:13,120
After my parents died,

5
00:01:14,840 --> 00:01:16,560
I had to keep my brother alive.

6
00:01:17,430 --> 00:01:18,680
We had nothing left.

7
00:01:21,280 --> 00:01:21,950
Back then

8
00:01:22,430 --> 00:01:25,870
I worked as an assistant at a nonprofit

9
00:01:25,920 --> 00:01:26,760
focused on adolescent mental health.

10
00:01:28,040 --> 00:01:29,640
I had access to university resources
across the province.

11
00:01:32,120 --> 00:01:33,510
Sun Jiahao found me

12
00:01:35,350 --> 00:01:36,510
and asked me to screen for

13
00:01:36,760 --> 00:01:37,680
young people with clean backgrounds,

14
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:39,760
deeply troubled families,

15
00:01:40,230 --> 00:01:41,710
and financial difficulties.

16
00:01:43,840 --> 00:01:44,710
Did you know at the time

17
00:01:44,710 --> 00:01:46,430
he wanted those girls as surrogates?

18
00:01:51,040 --> 00:01:52,150
Not at first.

19
00:01:54,150 --> 00:01:55,560
By the time I found out,
it was too late.

20
00:01:58,070 --> 00:01:59,310
Besides providing their information,

21
00:01:59,430 --> 00:02:00,710
what else did you do for him?

22
00:02:02,710 --> 00:02:03,710
Sometimes,

23
00:02:03,920 --> 00:02:06,920
girls who had agreed to be surrogates
would change their minds or resist.

24
00:02:07,920 --> 00:02:09,190
I would counsel them.

25
00:02:11,030 --> 00:02:11,840
Or,

26
00:02:13,120 --> 00:02:17,080
if a pregnant woman or new mother
had psychological problems,

27
00:02:17,710 --> 00:02:18,960
I dealt with those too.

28
00:02:22,630 --> 00:02:23,520
I've hurt him

29
00:02:27,710 --> 00:02:28,430
and my brother.

30
00:02:31,280 --> 00:02:32,080
Officer,

31
00:02:32,960 --> 00:02:34,310
can I see Han Ning?

32
00:02:35,870 --> 00:02:36,710
Why do you want to see him?

33
00:02:39,710 --> 00:02:40,680
There's something

34
00:02:41,630 --> 00:02:42,560
I want to tell him.

35
00:02:44,710 --> 00:02:45,960
He can't see you now.

36
00:02:46,240 --> 00:02:47,120
He's hurt.

37
00:02:47,280 --> 00:02:49,710
First, tell us
what chemical was found in his body.

38
00:02:55,310 --> 00:02:56,520
Alpha-isophenolphthalein.

39
00:03:05,520 --> 00:03:06,560
Alpha-isophenolphthalein?

40
00:03:07,910 --> 00:03:09,080
According to Ding Lan,

41
00:03:09,630 --> 00:03:11,400
after the Jiang Li case,

42
00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:13,630
Sun Jiahao feared the police
would trace it to him.

43
00:03:14,470 --> 00:03:15,240
He was especially worried
about Han Ning,

44
00:03:15,430 --> 00:03:17,240
who kept investigating
what happened seven years ago.

45
00:03:17,870 --> 00:03:20,280
So Sun Jiahao pressured Ding Lan

46
00:03:20,280 --> 00:03:21,630
to stop Han Ning from investigating.

47
00:03:22,840 --> 00:03:23,960
Ding Lan used this drug

48
00:03:24,360 --> 00:03:25,030
to make sure Han Ning

49
00:03:25,190 --> 00:03:25,960
could never be a police officer.

50
00:03:27,240 --> 00:03:30,360
It's a new drug developed abroad
to treat anxiety.

51
00:03:31,030 --> 00:03:31,910
In large doses,

52
00:03:32,240 --> 00:03:34,310
it can cause hallucinations
and even memory loss.

53
00:03:35,840 --> 00:03:38,080
If that happens to Han Ning,

54
00:03:40,150 --> 00:03:41,630
he can never be a police officer again.

55
00:03:43,080 --> 00:03:43,470
Brother Jun,

56
00:03:44,310 --> 00:03:45,080
can you help him?

57
00:03:50,150 --> 00:03:51,750
Now that we know the compound,
we can treat him.

58
00:03:52,840 --> 00:03:53,710
We can inject

59
00:03:54,310 --> 00:03:55,310
the corresponding antagonist.

60
00:04:42,360 --> 00:04:42,830
Sis.

61
00:04:44,510 --> 00:04:45,510
I want to rest for a while.

62
00:04:49,430 --> 00:04:51,310
Weren't you going to that mountain?

63
00:04:53,120 --> 00:04:54,120
It's still a long way.

64
00:04:56,750 --> 00:04:57,870
I've been walking for seven years.

65
00:04:59,920 --> 00:05:00,600
I don't think

66
00:05:01,830 --> 00:05:02,870
I can walk that far.

67
00:05:07,510 --> 00:05:08,480
We're almost there.

68
00:05:09,160 --> 00:05:10,510
Are you really giving up now?

69
00:05:14,510 --> 00:05:15,160
I'm exhausted.

70
00:05:17,430 --> 00:05:18,070
I missed you.

71
00:05:20,510 --> 00:05:21,680
Then come home with me.

72
00:05:23,920 --> 00:05:24,270
Okay.

73
00:05:25,270 --> 00:05:26,000
I'll come home with you.

74
00:05:32,160 --> 00:05:34,430
But only when we
reach the highest mountain

75
00:05:35,430 --> 00:05:37,070
can we find our way home.

76
00:05:55,310 --> 00:05:56,680
Doctor!

77
00:05:56,680 --> 00:05:57,630
He's moving!

78
00:06:20,240 --> 00:06:21,160
Everything has been done

79
00:06:21,430 --> 00:06:22,630
as you instructed.

80
00:06:23,040 --> 00:06:23,390
Mm.

81
00:06:30,240 --> 00:06:31,830
Let this matter end here.

82
00:06:32,120 --> 00:06:32,720
But...

83
00:06:32,920 --> 00:06:34,600
that police officer woke up.

84
00:06:36,310 --> 00:06:37,120
What?

85
00:06:38,950 --> 00:06:40,480
Jiahao could never make up his mind.

86
00:06:41,240 --> 00:06:42,120
Always wavering,

87
00:06:42,630 --> 00:06:43,510
he was no match for his opponent.

88
00:06:44,920 --> 00:06:46,750
Only when cornered did he know

89
00:06:47,870 --> 00:06:49,270
to sacrifice the rook to save the king.

90
00:06:51,160 --> 00:06:53,160
He was only a pawn.

91
00:06:53,920 --> 00:06:55,560
You're the king.

92
00:06:58,270 --> 00:06:58,920
Tianci.

93
00:07:02,510 --> 00:07:03,310
Come here.
Come here.

94
00:07:05,870 --> 00:07:06,560
Give that to me.

95
00:07:10,070 --> 00:07:11,510
Throw this away.

96
00:07:17,560 --> 00:07:18,800
Do you know what this is?

97
00:07:19,870 --> 00:07:20,310
A cannon.

98
00:07:26,950 --> 00:07:28,560
I knew something was off with you.

99
00:07:29,560 --> 00:07:31,430
I never thought
you'd cause such a huge mess.

100
00:07:33,270 --> 00:07:35,360
You can't judge people by appearances.

101
00:07:35,920 --> 00:07:37,870
They may look perfectly respectable.

102
00:07:38,390 --> 00:07:41,000
But if Ding Lan's brother hadn't died,

103
00:07:42,040 --> 00:07:42,560
she probably

104
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:44,070
would have come after you too.

105
00:07:46,750 --> 00:07:47,190
Then...

106
00:07:47,630 --> 00:07:50,070
What do the autopsy reports
on Sun Jiahao and Ding Wei say?

107
00:07:50,920 --> 00:07:52,480
Pretty much what we inferred
at the scene.

108
00:07:53,160 --> 00:07:55,560
Ding Wei tried to kill Sun Jiahao
to avenge his sister,

109
00:07:55,560 --> 00:07:57,560
but Sun Jiahao killed him instead.

110
00:07:58,430 --> 00:07:59,950
Sun Jiahao was also injured.

111
00:08:00,510 --> 00:08:01,750
He lost too much blood

112
00:08:02,160 --> 00:08:02,950
and died too.

113
00:08:03,560 --> 00:08:04,750
All those deaths

114
00:08:05,870 --> 00:08:07,510
and the illegal surrogacy ring...

115
00:08:08,360 --> 00:08:09,270
He was behind them all.

116
00:08:09,510 --> 00:08:09,950
Then...

117
00:08:11,120 --> 00:08:11,920
What about my sister?

118
00:08:13,430 --> 00:08:14,560
There's no connection.

119
00:08:15,270 --> 00:08:18,000
The DNA results from the remains
on Cuiping Mountain

120
00:08:18,680 --> 00:08:20,070
are all back.

121
00:08:20,630 --> 00:08:21,430
None matched Han Shuang.

122
00:08:30,360 --> 00:08:30,680
Ah.

123
00:08:31,240 --> 00:08:32,030
What are you doing?

124
00:08:35,750 --> 00:08:37,080
Get back here and lie down.

125
00:08:45,750 --> 00:08:46,360
Have some water.

126
00:08:49,510 --> 00:08:49,910
Drink some.

127
00:08:49,910 --> 00:08:50,120
Thanks.

128
00:08:54,390 --> 00:08:55,080
Hurry.

129
00:08:55,270 --> 00:08:56,440
Don't let your senior catch you.

130
00:08:56,750 --> 00:08:56,960
Okay.

131
00:09:06,960 --> 00:09:08,670
After Sun Jiahao opened the door,

132
00:09:08,840 --> 00:09:12,120
Ding Wei ambushed and stabbed him.

133
00:09:13,910 --> 00:09:15,240
But he hadn't expected

134
00:09:16,080 --> 00:09:17,440
Ding Wei to be too weak

135
00:09:17,960 --> 00:09:19,720
to inflict a fatal wound.

136
00:09:22,480 --> 00:09:22,960
The photo.

137
00:09:39,270 --> 00:09:43,120
When Ding Wei weakened,
Sun Jiahao wrested the weapon from him

138
00:09:43,720 --> 00:09:46,960
and slit his throat, killing him.

139
00:09:48,670 --> 00:09:49,630
If that's what happened,

140
00:09:50,630 --> 00:09:52,120
then why did Sun Jiahao die?

141
00:09:59,150 --> 00:10:00,440
Do you need a break?

142
00:10:00,510 --> 00:10:01,320
I'm fine.

143
00:10:01,960 --> 00:10:02,750
The report?

144
00:10:05,840 --> 00:10:06,960
The report says

145
00:10:07,030 --> 00:10:08,200
Sun Jiahao died from

146
00:10:08,910 --> 00:10:10,240
excessive blood loss.

147
00:10:21,870 --> 00:10:23,320
He suffered seven stab wounds.

148
00:10:23,550 --> 00:10:26,240
Several wounds measured
no more than five centimeters deep.

149
00:10:27,750 --> 00:10:29,320
Only one was fatal.

150
00:10:30,630 --> 00:10:31,870
It pierced his spine.

151
00:10:32,240 --> 00:10:35,670
That would require
more than 50 kilograms of force.

152
00:10:38,120 --> 00:10:41,480
You mean
Ding Wei didn't kill Sun Jiahao?

153
00:10:43,720 --> 00:10:44,750
Ding Wei didn't have that strength.

154
00:10:45,150 --> 00:10:47,870
He couldn't even help his drunk sister
into a car.

155
00:10:48,120 --> 00:10:49,840
How could he possibly
have killed Sun Jiahao?

156
00:11:26,550 --> 00:11:27,240
There was

157
00:11:28,200 --> 00:11:29,200
a third person in this room.

158
00:11:30,480 --> 00:11:31,670
The killer was highly skilled.

159
00:11:32,600 --> 00:11:33,790
They left no fingerprints

160
00:11:34,150 --> 00:11:36,270
and even avoided every bloodstain.

161
00:11:36,750 --> 00:11:38,510
They knew exactly how
to evade detection.

162
00:11:39,910 --> 00:11:41,390
This is the person behind Sun Jiahao,

163
00:11:41,870 --> 00:11:43,960
someone never before on our radar.

164
00:12:25,580 --> 00:12:27,640
♪I stand in a fire-tempered jungle♪

165
00:12:27,640 --> 00:12:29,580
♪Withered leaves fall
as my strength runs dry♪

166
00:12:29,580 --> 00:12:31,490
♪Dust swirls as I clench my fists♪

167
00:12:31,490 --> 00:12:33,300
♪I strategize, my faith my armor♪

168
00:12:33,300 --> 00:12:35,640
♪My defiance spills onto concrete♪

169
00:12:35,640 --> 00:12:38,060
♪Even thick fog can't hide
my clear gaze♪

170
00:12:41,210 --> 00:12:43,110
♪Let neon turn to thorns♪

171
00:12:43,110 --> 00:12:45,010
♪Flying low as the stars shift and turn♪

172
00:12:45,010 --> 00:12:46,960
♪Escape the maze,
transcend the challenge♪

173
00:12:46,960 --> 00:12:49,080
♪The meter starts, breaking the silence♪

174
00:12:49,110 --> 00:12:51,090
♪A beam cuts through
a crack in the wall♪

175
00:12:51,090 --> 00:12:53,250
♪This rhythm and noise
echo through the streets♪

176
00:12:56,850 --> 00:13:00,330
♪Don't be afraid. No one will answer♪

177
00:13:00,330 --> 00:13:03,690
♪Why is that child crying?♪

178
00:13:03,930 --> 00:13:06,400
♪The shrinking scar on my arm♪

179
00:13:06,400 --> 00:13:08,010
♪Means I've grown up♪

180
00:13:08,010 --> 00:13:11,160
♪You can trust me when I say that♪

181
00:13:11,160 --> 00:13:14,650
♪The wound still aches♪

182
00:13:15,050 --> 00:13:19,410
♪Like a biting winter♪

183
00:13:19,410 --> 00:13:22,670
♪But a spark still glows♪

